// wdoc section: Sites & Templates.
page wdoc_sites { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Sites & Templates"

  p "A `site` block configures one output site — its template, title, theme, and navigation. A document can declare several sites; each page joins one or more via its `sites` field."

  h2 "Fields"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Field"             | "Meaning" |
      | "`default_template`" | "`:webpage` (header + top nav) or `:book` (sidebar + TOC)" |
      | "`title`"           | "Site title shown in the header / sidebar" |
      | "`root`"            | "When `true`, this site renders at `/` (others go under `/<site>/`)" |
      | "`theme`"           | "Built-in colour theme — see [Themes](wdoc_themes)" |
      | "`accent`"          | "Symbol naming the accent hue (`:red`..`:pink`); default `:blue`" |
      | "`theme_toggle`"    | "When `true`, adds a light/dark toggle button" |
      | "`menu { … }`"      | "Top navbar entries for the `webpage` template" |
      | "`toc { … }`"       | "Chapter tree for the `book` template" |
  }

  h2 "webpage template"

  p "Hugo-style site header, sticky top navbar built from `menu`, and a reading column."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
site marketing {
  default_template = :webpage
  title            = "My project"
  root             = true
  theme            = nord
  menu {
    item "Home"     { page = index }
    item "Docs"     { href = "docs/" }
    item "More" {
      item "About"   { page = about }
      item "Contact" { page = contact }
    }
    item "Source"   { href = "https://github.com/example/proj" }
  }
}
WCL
  }
  p "Menu items use `page = <name>` for in-site links (validated against pages in this site) or `href = \"…\"` for external or cross-site URLs. Nested `item`s become dropdown groups."

  h2 "book template"

  p "mdBook-style fixed left sidebar with nested chapters and current-chapter highlight; reading column on the right."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
site docs {
  default_template = :book
  title            = "Project Docs"
  theme            = nord
  theme_toggle     = true
  toc {
    chapter "Intro"        { page = index }
    chapter "Guide" {
      chapter "Setup"      { page = setup }
      chapter "First run"  { page = first_run }
    }
  }
}
WCL
  }
  p "Chapters nest to any depth. A `chapter` with no `page =` is a grouping heading. A `chapter` pointing at an unknown page is a build error."

  p "Next: [Pages](wdoc_pages)."
}
